This is interesting because the file watcher shouldn't have started watching that directory yet. It should init the file watcher lower dow when it does this:

```ts
        const booted = await Instance.provide({
          directory: info.directory,
          init: InstanceBootstrap,
          fn: () => undefined,
        })
```

which will call `InstanceBootstrap` which bootstraps the worktree instance, which starts the file watcher. The hard reset is done before this, any chance you can figure out why the file watcher is watching those files?

@michaeldwan this looks sensible, but one question: isn't the "write" fix only applicable in the case where you create a git worktree outside of opencode, in a project that you have never opened opencode in before, and start opencode in the worktree?

I fixed the read case with the assumption in mind that opencode has always generated and cached the project in in the local project's `.git` dir. You're right that we should the write case too, but it's a rare edge case right?

Also switching to `HEAD` for rev-list makes a lot of sense. I will confirm tomorrow morning that it's works as expected, but that's a great suggestion
